      "technicals_tldr": {
        "path": "wiki/tickers/DIS/technicals.md",
        "mode": "tldr",
        "content": "As of May 4, 2026 (run `20260504_221111`), the April 30 breakout has been almost entirely retraced: price fell from the $104.83 post-breakout high back to $101.31 (hourly) \u2014 near the hard stop at $101.00. The daily trend remains technically intact (ADX 38.73, +DI 31.91 dominating -DI 19.30) but EMA structure is tangled \u2014 all four short-term EMAs clustered within $0.80. Hourly price is below all EMAs with -DI leading +DI. Earnings risk manager blackout enforced (May 6 pre-market, 2 days). Prior setup type \"pre-earnings momentum breakout\" has been replaced by \"near-stop pullback consolidation \u2014 watch only.\"\n\n---",
        "last_updated": "2026-05-04",
        "stale": false
      },
      "regime_tldr": {
        "path": "wiki/macro/regime.md",
        "mode": "tldr",
        "content": "**Partial risk-on recovery on May 5, but Iran tail risk unresolved.** The May 4 risk-off shock (Iran missile strikes on US warship near Jask) has partially unwound: S&P 500 and Nasdaq recovered on May 5, with Nasdaq reaching an intraday ATH. However, the Iran-UAE/Strait of Hormuz conflict has escalated further \u2014 missiles and drones targeted the UAE while Strait of Hormuz closure risk remains active, keeping oil above $102/bbl. The macro regime is best characterized as **mixed-to-cautiously-bullish**: solid earnings are providing a near-term offset, but geopolitical left-tail risk has not been removed. Hawkish Fed leadership transition on May 15 adds policy uncertainty. [source: web_research/META.json macro_context, run 20260505_140723]",
        "last_updated": "2026-05-05",
        "stale": false
      },
      "lessons_full": {
        "path": "wiki/meta/lessons.md",
